JSON<pre><code>{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "gzkit_version": "&lt;X.Y.Z&gt;",
  "surfaces": {
    "skills": ["&lt;slug&gt;/SKILL.md", ...],
    "rules": ["&lt;filename&gt;.md", ...],
    "personas": ["&lt;filename&gt;.md", ...],
    "templates": ["&lt;filename&gt;.md", ...]
  }
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>schema_version</code>: format version of this manifest. Currently <code>1.0</code>. Bumped   if surface taxonomy changes (e.g. new surface added that requires a new   enumeration shape).</li> <li><code>gzkit_version</code>: gzkit release the manifest was authored against. Used by   diagnostics to flag manifest/wheel mismatch.</li> <li><code>surfaces</code>: dict of surface name to list of surface-relative paths.</li> <li>Skill entries are <code>"&lt;slug&gt;/SKILL.md"</code> (relative to <code>src/gzkit/skills/</code>).</li> <li>Rule, persona, and template entries are bare filenames (relative to     <code>src/gzkit/&lt;surface&gt;/</code>).</li> </ul>

Bash<pre><code>uv run gz status --table
uv run gz adr status ADR-&lt;X.Y.Z&gt; --json
uv run gz adr report
uv run gz state --json
uv run gz adr audit-check ADR-&lt;X.Y.Z&gt;
uv run gz adr fidelity ADR-&lt;X.Y.Z&gt;   # bound gate; closeout + audit invoke it (ADR-0.0.73)
uv run gz adr covers-check ADR-&lt;X.Y.Z&gt;
uv run gz gates --adr ADR-&lt;X.Y.Z&gt;
uv run gz obpi status OBPI-&lt;X.Y.Z-NN&gt;
uv run gz roles
uv run gz personas list               # List agent personas
uv run gz personas list --json         # List personas as JSON
</code></pre>

